---
// Traduction anglaise de /a-propos/ — reprise du contenu déjà traduit sur
// l'ancien site (src/pages/en/about.astro).
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/legacy-article.css";

const title = "Stéphane, Interim Management Consultant, Tech & AI";
const description =
  "30 years of operational leadership in tech: Software, Retail, Telco. Interim manager for mid-market companies and scale-ups. Measurable results, not reports.";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: "Stéphane Dinepro",
  jobTitle: "Interim Management Consultant, Tech & AI",
  description,
  url: "https://izybiz.fr/en/about/",
  sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/sdine/", "https://izybiz.fr"],
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Izybiz", url: "https://izybiz.fr" },
  knowsAbout: [
    "Interim Management",
    "Operational Transformation",
    "AI Integration",
    "Business Unit Leadership",
    "Scale-up Operations",
  ],
};
---

<Layout lang="en" title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/en/about/">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <main class="legacy-article legacy-article--profile">
    <article class="legacy-article__article">
      <span class="legacy-article__kicker">About</span>
      <h1 class="legacy-article__title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="legacy-article__lede">{description}</p>

      <div class="legacy-article__stats">
        <div class="legacy-article__stat legacy-article__stat--yellow">
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-value">30 years</p>
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-label">of operational leadership in tech</p>
        </div>
        <div class="legacy-article__stat legacy-article__stat--blue">
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-value">9</p>
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-label">major accounts, from Crédit Agricole to OVH</p>
        </div>
        <div class="legacy-article__stat legacy-article__stat--lavender">
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-value">3</p>
          <p class="legacy-article__stat-label">sectors: Software, Retail, Telecom</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="legacy-article__body">
        <p>
          No remote recommendations. An executive who steps in, works with your
          teams, and stays accountable for your results all the way to the end.
        </p>
        <p>That's the only thing Izybiz offers.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Where did this path start?</h2>
        <p>
          I started in luxury hospitality. In the late 90s, I tried to convince my
          general manager that the internet could become a communication channel for
          the hotel. His response, word for word: he didn't want to roll out email
          just so secretaries could gossip all day, and he didn't believe for a
          second that technology could improve his relationship with guests.
        </p>
        <p>
          I changed industries the next day. No bitterness, just the certainty that
          I couldn't work somewhere the future was treated with suspicion.
        </p>
        <p>
          I joined the launch of The Phone House in France and Belgium. A startup
          riding the mobile wave at a time when nobody quite knew what a mobile phone
          was going to change in people's lives. Then different sectors, different
          companies, different contexts, always the same role.
        </p>
        <p>
          Technical manager first, business unit director next, CEO last. Software,
          Retail, E-commerce, Last-mile logistics, Telecommunications. Commercial
          development, team mergers, transformation projects, delivered in-house or
          as an external partner for Crédit Agricole, Bouygues Telecom, SFR, Canal+,
          SNCF, PSA, Carrefour, OVH, Engie, and in startups.
        </p>
        <p>
          That path, I chose it. Walk into something complex, structure it, get it
          running, then move on once it holds.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Why Izybiz?</h2>
        <p>
          The decision to create Izybiz came out of a mission in West Africa. A telco
          operator had contacted me to revive a super app that had been gathering
          dust for two years. The project was there, the teams were there. What was
          missing was someone to hold the execution together. I took the mission. But
          right before it kicked off, I realised that once again I'd leave it for
          another project, another adventure. I figured I might as well make that a
          clear model.
        </p>
        <p class="legacy-article__pull">
          "People call you instinctively when they have a problem to solve. And
          for you, their problem is rarely insurmountable, it just looks simple."
          <em>A former colleague, on why the name stuck: Izy. Biz.</em>
        </p>
        <p>
          When you bring in Izybiz, you're working with someone who has already
          navigated what you're going through, not someone who will figure it out
          at your expense.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>What do I actually do, and what don't I?</h2>
        <p>I'm an interim manager, not a consultant.</p>
        <p>
          A consultant delivers recommendations. An interim manager takes on a
          role, such as CEO, COO or CDO, and actually performs it, with your
          teams, on your challenges. They own the results. They leave when the
          organisation can stand on its own.
        </p>
        <p>
          My dual expertise covers two types of missions that most interim managers
          can't deliver together:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Operational transformation:</strong> when an organisation needs to
          change pace, structure, or direction. Pre-Series B scale-up, turnaround of
          a struggling business unit, steering a drifting transformation, stepping
          into a vacant leadership role.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI integration in business:</strong> when AI projects keep failing
          for lack of governance and an operational leader. From framing use cases
          through to production deployment, with a trained team and workflows that
          hold over time.
        </p>
        <p>Those two competencies rarely come in the same person. That's Izybiz's differentiator.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>How do I work?</h2>
        <p>
          Every mission starts with a rigorous scoping phase: stakes, constraints,
          KPIs. No flying blind from day one.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm embedded in the teams, not hovering above them. Decisions are made
          with the data available, not while waiting for the perfect report. KPIs
          are tracked monthly and every result is documented at the end of each
          mission. ROI is traceable. That's a requirement, not a promise.
        </p>
        <p>
          The organisation leaves the mission fully independent. No dependency
          created, no continuation of services sold on the way out.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Which sectors do I work in?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Software & SaaS:</strong> operational scaling, enterprise churn
          reduction, delivery structuring, AI integration.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Retail & E-commerce:</strong> operations transformation,
          digitalisation, last-mile, commercial performance management.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Telecommunications:</strong> major account management, business
          unit transformation, commercial performance, breakthrough projects.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also work outside France, in particular across West Africa, where I've
          run several missions on launch, structuring, and digital integration
          challenges.
        </p>

        <div class="legacy-article__final">
          <h2 class="legacy-article__final-title">Ready to talk?</h2>
          <p class="legacy-article__final-text">
            A situation can't be summed up in a few lines. Book a 30-minute call,
            with no pitch and no commitment, to clarify whether your situation
            calls for interim management and whether Izybiz is the right fit.
          </p>
          <a class="legacy-article__cta" href="/en/contact/" data-cta="closing-cta">Book a call</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
